                <head>130. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>The meeting of the Ministerial Council of the Organization for Economic
                    Cooperation and Development was held in Paris November 24–25, 1966. For text of
                    two briefing papers prepared for the meeting, see <ref target="#d128">Documents
                        128</ref> and <ref target="#d129">129</ref>. Under Secretary of State for
                    Political Affairs Eugene V. Rostow headed the U.S. Delegation. For texts of
                    Rostow’s statements on economic policy and East-West relations on November 24,
                    and development assistance and trade on November 25, see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, January 2, 1967, pages 19–27. Text of the
                    communique is ibid., pages 27–28.</p>
                <p>For an account of the discussion on development aid problems on November 25, see
                        <ref target="#d131">Document 131</ref>. Telegrams summarizing discussions on
                    trade with the less-developed nations, economic policy, and East-West relations
                    on November 24 and 25 are in Department of State, Central Files, OECD 3.</p>
                <p>A summary and appraisal of this OECD meeting is in <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Current Economic Developments</hi>, Issue No. 768, December 6, 1966, pages
                    6–11. (Washington National Records Center, RG 59, E/CBA/REP Files: FRC 72 A
                    6248, <hi rendition="#italic">Current Economic Developments</hi>) The evaluation
                    of discussions on development and the world food problem is also in Issue No.
                    768, pages 9–10.</p>
                <p>Additional documentation on the meeting, which includes many other background and
                    briefing papers, is ibid., RG 286, DAC Material: FRC 70 A 5922, Meetings—OECD
                    Ministerial November 24–25, 1966; and Department of State, Conference Files: Lot
                    67 D 586, CF 101A.</p>
